## Summary

✅ **DO:**
- Use Tailwind 4.1 `@theme` directive in CSS
- Follow three-layer architecture: Utilities → Controls → Components
- Use CSS classes for reusable controls (.btn-primary, .input, .card)
- Use utility classes for layout and spacing
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Container queries for component-level responsiveness
- Use `[ngClass]` or `[class]` for dynamic classes in Angular
- Use `:host` for styling component host elements
- Scope styles with component styleUrls when appropriate

❌ **DON'T:**
- Use old Tailwind 3.x configuration style
- Put all styles inline (use CSS classes for controls)
- Use CSS classes for layout (use utilities)
- Desktop-first responsive design
- Skip responsive design considerations
- Use `class` (Angular)